From 01f41b4328d4f2243bd463b602f6af7040c4865c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:49:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Items 16, 17, 18 plus the carried-forward composition
 limitation and an F0-specific K. Item 16: new score_book.py scoring an
 operator-assembled book on Appendix B, importing every estimator from
 selection.py rather than reimplementing any, with a non-zero exit naming the
 breach on stdout and an append-only book_scored.jsonl carrying book_sha256,
 input_sha, code_sha and UTC timestamp as an attestation record exempt from
 the determinism rule. Item 17: wf_selection.book_arm_from_valid applies VALID
 on the training segment alone per split, scores its members on test and
 ratios against the seeded null, and the artifact states it certifies the
 catalogue inclusion rule and not any book. Item 18: the denominator is now
 n_traded rather than n_included so a signal that never fired on test is not
 counted as a failure, PERSIST_DEFINITION and DENOMINATOR_DEFINITION are
 module constants, and assert_arms_agree aborts if the arms disagree. Carried
 forward: the null matches rarity but not condition composition, recorded as
 intended rather than closed, since matching it would make the null a
 near-copy of the population. null_k_for gives F0 K=500 with the reasoning
 that the remedy for a blank is a larger K and never a wider tolerance. A
 never-called sweep found depth_yield_per_signal and same_signal_refire_rate
 defined and unconsumed; both are now emitted in the DepthYield grid.

